@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple use case diagram — one Customer actor associated with three use cases inside an ATM system boundary.
'   usecase:      Teach actor (stick figure), use case (ellipse), system boundary (rectangle), and association.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       Banking / ATM
' ============================================================================
title Example Use Case Diagram - Simple ATM

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' A USE CASE DIAGRAM captures functional requirements from an ACTOR's point of
' view.  Core concepts:
'   - ACTOR: an external role (human or system) drawn as a stick figure.
'   - USE CASE: a unit of behaviour worth describing, drawn as an ellipse.
'   - SYSTEM BOUNDARY: a rectangle that scopes WHICH use cases belong to the
'     system under design.
'   - ASSOCIATION: a solid line between an actor and a use case it
#     participates in (no arrowhead by convention, or an open arrow).
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

left to right direction

' ACTOR — external role interacting with the system.
actor "Customer" as cust

' SYSTEM BOUNDARY — the rectangle scopes what the ATM is responsible for.
rectangle "ATM System" {

  ' USE CASES — ellipses, one unit of observable behaviour each.
  usecase "Withdraw Cash"    as uc1
  usecase "Check Balance"    as uc2
  usecase "Deposit Funds"    as uc3
}

' ASSOCIATIONS — the Customer participates in each use case.
cust --> uc1
cust --> uc2
cust --> uc3

note right of uc2
  <b>How to read this diagram</b>
  • Stick figure = ACTOR (Customer).
  • Ellipse = USE CASE (Check Balance).
  • Rectangle = SYSTEM BOUNDARY.
  • Solid line = ASSOCIATION
    (actor participates in the use case).
  Use cases answer "WHAT does the system
  do for this actor?" — not HOW.
end note

@enduml
